  "summary": "The study prepared small monolayer Ti3C2Tx by LiF/HCl etching, delamination, and probe sonication, then formed porous foams using sacrificial positively charged PS spheres. Seven electrochemically benchmarked electrode materials with printed performance data were identified: a pristine MXene-film control, three 6:1 MXene:PS template-size foams, and three MXene/CNT composite foams. MX6PS310-A was the best reported capacitance performer, delivering 474 F g\u22121 and 1121 F cm\u22123 at 2 mV s\u22121 in 1 m H2SO4. The authors also fabricated MX1PS310, MX2PS310, MX4PS310, and MX8PS310 ratio-series films/foams, but the supplied text gives no individual capacitance values for them; they are discussed only as optimization screening samples and are therefore not entered as separately quantified electrodes."
